# Services registered with the legacy servicemanager.
#
# The legacy servicemanager (the one that runs on this device) resolves
# service names through plat_service_contexts + nonplat_service_contexts.
# CAF only ships the mapping for the two services below in
# device/qcom/sepolicy/common/vndservice_contexts, which is the file
# used by vndservicemanager.  Without the entries here both names fall
# through to the plat catch-all "default_android_service" and the
# registration is rejected with
#
#   avc: denied { add } for service=vendor.qcom.PeripheralManager
#      scontext=u:r:per_mgr:s0 tcontext=u:object_r:default_android_service:s0
#      tclass=service_manager
#
# The types themselves are declared by CAF in
# device/qcom/sepolicy/common/vndservice.te; service.te adds the
# service_manager_type attribute they need to be usable here.
vendor.qcom.PeripheralManager                   u:object_r:per_mgr_service:s0
com.qualcomm.qti.qseeproxy                      u:object_r:qseeproxy_service:s0
